A lathe operator writes a whole-number tolerance with a decimal point and nothing after it. Which value does the printer show?
class Lathe {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.print(5.);
    }
}

A half-step tolerance is written with the decimal point in front of the digit. Which value reaches the printer?
class HalfStep {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.print(.5);
    }
}

A span of one thousand millimetres is written in scientific notation. Which value reaches the printer?
class Span {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.print(1e3);
    }
}

A tolerance of one hundredth of a millimetre is written with a negative exponent. Which value reaches the printer?
class Tol {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.print(1E-2);
    }
}

A duty cycle of two and a half percent is written as a single precision literal. Which value reaches the printer?
class Duty {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        float d = 2.5f;
        System.out.print(d);
    }
}

A valve mask is written in hexadecimal with an upper-case prefix and lower-case digits. Which value reaches the printer?
class ValveBank {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int idx = 0xFf;
        System.out.print(idx);
    }
}

A legacy configuration file encodes a permission mask with a leading zero and no prefix. Which value reaches the printer?
class PermMask {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int mask = 0777;
        System.out.print(mask);
    }
}

A parity mask is written with thirty two one bits and no suffix. Which value reaches the printer?
class Parity {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int all = 0b11111111111111111111111111111111;
        System.out.print(all);
    }
}

A device mask of 0xFFFFFFFF is stored in an int. Which value reaches the printer?
class DevMask {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int m = 0xFFFFFFFF;
        System.out.print(m);
    }
}

A checksum mask of sixty four hexadecimal F digits is stored in a long. Which value reaches the printer?
class Checksum {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        long cs = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFL;
        System.out.print(cs);
    }
}

A port number is written in hexadecimal with a separator every digit. Which value reaches the printer?
class PortNo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int port = 0x1_2_3;
        System.out.print(port);
    }
}

A nibble mask is written in binary with one separator per nibble. Which value reaches the printer?
class Nibble {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int m = 0b1111_0000;
        System.out.print(m);
    }
}

A viscosity figure is written as a decimal literal with separators around the point. Which value reaches the printer?
class Viscosity {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        double v = 1_0.2_5;
        System.out.print(v);
    }
}

A very large span is written with separators in both the mantissa and the exponent. Which text reaches the printer?
class Huge {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        double d = 1_0e1_0;
        System.out.print(d);
    }
}

A ledger prints the code unit of a tab character held in a char. Which number reaches the printer?
class TabCode {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        char c = '\t';
        System.out.print((int) c);
    }
}

A terminal eraser prompt prints the code unit of a backspace character. Which number reaches the printer?
class Bspace {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        char c = '\b';
        System.out.print((int) c);
    }
}

A page break in a text file is written with a form feed escape. Which number does the printer report?
class PageBreak {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        char c = '\f';
        System.out.print((int) c);
    }
}

An old terminal log separates records with a carriage return escape held in a char. Which number does the printer report?
class CrLog {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        char c = '\r';
        System.out.print((int) c);
    }
}

A sentinel char is written with the one digit octal escape. Which number does the printer report?
class Sentinel {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        char c = '\0';
        System.out.print((int) c);
    }
}

A grade char is written with the three digit octal escape for sixty five. Which number does the printer report?
class Grade {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        char c = '\101';
        System.out.print((int) c);
    }
}

A delimiter field holds a single quote mark written as an escape inside a char literal. Which character does the printer show?
class Delim {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        char c = '\'';
        System.out.print(c);
    }
}

A field holds a single double quote mark inside a char literal. Which character does the printer show?
class Quote {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        char c = '"';
        System.out.print(c);
    }
}

A path separator field holds a backslash written as an escape inside a char literal. Which character does the printer show?
class Sep {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        char c = '\\';
        System.out.print(c);
    }
}

A field name is written with a letter, a newline, and a letter, where the newline is written as an escape. How many characters does the string hold?
class FieldName {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String s = "a\nb";
        System.out.print(s.length());
    }
}

A newline char is written with a two digit octal escape. Which number does the printer report?
class NlCode {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        char c = '\12';
        System.out.print((int) c);
    }
}

A lower case vowel is written with the three digit octal escape for its code unit. Which character does the printer show?
class Vowel {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        char c = '\141';
        System.out.print(c);
    }
}

A programmer writes an octal escape whose value does not fit a char. What happens when this program is compiled?
class TooWide {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        char c = '\400';
        System.out.print((int) c);
    }
}

A checksum adds one to the code unit of a newline char held in a char. Which number does the printer report?
class Check {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int v = '\n' + 1;
        System.out.print(v);
    }
}

A grade char is written with a unicode escape for code unit 65. Which number does the printer report?
class UniGrade {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        char c = '\u0041';
        System.out.print((int) c);
    }
}

A shelf label is written with a unicode escape for code unit 66 in the middle of the text. Which character does the printer show in that position?
class UniLabel {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String s = "[\u0042]";
        System.out.print(s);
    }
}

An accented vowel is written with a unicode escape. Which number does the printer report for its code unit?
class Accent {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        char c = '\u00e9';
        System.out.print((int) c);
    }
}

A star rating is written as a surrogate pair of two unicode escapes. How many chars does the string hold?
class Star {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String s = "\uD83D\uDE00";
        System.out.print(s.length());
    }
}

A terminator char uses the unicode escape for the highest code unit. Which number does the printer report?
class Terminator {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        char c = '\uffff';
        System.out.print((int) c);
    }
}

A gain figure is written as a hexadecimal float with a one bit fraction. Which value reaches the printer?
class HexGain {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        double g = 0x1.8p1;
        System.out.print(g);
    }
}

A span figure is written as a hexadecimal float with a power of two exponent. Which value reaches the printer?
class HexSpan {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        double s = 0x1p4;
        System.out.print(s);
    }
}

A calibration figure is written as a hexadecimal float but the programmer left off the exponent. What happens when this program is compiled?
class NoExp {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        double c = 0x1.8;
        System.out.print(c);
    }
}

A motor ratio is written with an exponent and no decimal point, plus the single precision suffix. Which value reaches the printer?
class Ratio {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        float r = 1e1f;
        System.out.print(r);
    }
}

A baseline figure is written with the explicit double suffix. Which value reaches the printer?
class Baseline {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        double b = 1.0d;
        System.out.print(b);
    }
}

A total of one billion is written with separators and an explicit long suffix, then divided by three. Which value reaches the printer?
class LongGroups {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        long big = 1_000_000_000L;
        System.out.print(big / 3L);
    }
}

A wide parity mask is written with thirty five one bits and an explicit long suffix. Which value reaches the printer?
class WideParity {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        long m = 0b11111111111111111111111111111111111L;
        System.out.print(m);
    }
}

A register address is written as the highest positive hexadecimal int. Which value reaches the printer?
class RegAddr {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int addr = 0x7FFFFFFF;
        System.out.print(addr);
    }
}

A gate code must hold the character whose code unit is 9, written with the two digit octal escape. Which replacement of the marked line stores it that way?
class GateCode {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        char gate = 'a'; // <-- edit this line
        System.out.print((int) gate);
    }
}

A field value was meant to hold three characters, a letter, a tab, and a letter, but the program reports 4 because the backslash was doubled. Which replacement of the marked line makes the program print 3?
class FieldValue {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String field = "x\\ty"; // <-- edit this line
        System.out.print(field.length());
    }
}

A crate count of ten thousand must be written with one separator, and the marked line is the whole declaration. Which replacement of the marked line is legal?
class Crates {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int crates = 10000; // <-- edit this line
        System.out.print(crates);
    }
}

A gate label must be written as a four digit unicode escape so the source file stays plain ASCII. Which replacement of the marked line uses that form?
class GateLabel {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        char gate = 'a'; // <-- edit this line
        System.out.print(gate);
    }
}

A gain figure is written as a hex float but comes out as 4.0 when it should be 3.0. Which replacement of the marked line makes the program print 3.0?
class HexGain2 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        double g = 0x2p1; // <-- edit this line
        System.out.print(g);
    }
}

A motor ratio of ten must stay in single precision, and the marked line is the whole declaration. Which replacement of the marked line is legal?
class MotorRatio {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        float ratio = 1e1f; // <-- edit this line
        System.out.print(ratio);
    }
}

A tag was meant to print as id:Q, but it prints as id: followed by a backslash and four more characters, because the backslash was doubled in the source. Which replacement of the marked line makes the program print id:Q?
class TagText {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String tag = "id:\\u0051"; // <-- edit this line
        System.out.print(tag);
    }
}
